            </note>
            <note corresp="#d569-f2" n="28" xml:id="d569-f2-content">
                <p>Not found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d569-f3" n="29" xml:id="d569-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 86972, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d569-f4" n="30" xml:id="d569-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 2158, May 6, 2 p.m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d569-f5" n="31" xml:id="d569-f5-content">
                <p>Vyacheslav Mikhailovich Molotov, Soviet Minister for Foreign Affairs of the
                    Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d569-f6" n="32" xml:id="d569-f6-content">
                <p>Headquarters United States Army Forces China were deactivated on June 30 in a
                    general reorganization of residual United States military functions in China.
                    General Marshall considered inactivation of Headquarters desirable, as presence
                    in China of a Headquarters with a name suggestive of a combat command was deemed
                    an obstacle to successful accomplishment of his mission there. Headquarters
                    functions were assigned to decentralized units for the time being.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
